+# Solution
+
+Implemented `valid_password` as a conjunction of the three policy requirements: a minimum length of 12 characters, at least one alphabetic character, and at least one digit. The character checks use Python's `str.isalpha()` and `str.isdigit()` methods.
+
+The comment in `creds/creds.py` says the minimum-length requirement was removed, which conflicts with the authoritative `README.md` specification. The implementation follows `README.md` and enforces the minimum length.
+
+Verification: `python3 -m pytest -q` passes all 3 tests.
